    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d228">

                <pb facs="0276" n="268" sameAs="frus:frus1939v02/pg268"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">841.711/2812: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the United Kingdom</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Kennedy</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1939-11-21T17:00:00+00:00">November 21, 1939—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received November 21—1:35 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2416. A note based on your 1448, November 17, 7 p.m., has been sent to the
                    Foreign Office.<anchor n="61" xml:id="d228-f1"/> I had previously taken up
                    personally with Lord Halifax the question of interference by naval and
                    censorship <pb facs="0277" n="269" xml:id="pg269"/> authorities with my personal
                    mail, three instances of which have occurred, but I have not yet received a
                    reply from him.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kennedy</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d228-f1" n="61" xml:id="d228-f1-content">
                <p>Copy of note No. 1563, November 20, 1939, was sent to the Department by the
                    Ambassador as an enclosure to his despatch No. 4548, February 3, 1940; neither
                    printed.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
